WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:04.920
Hey there VisualPolitik community, what a
mess is going on in Africa!

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.670
The coup d'état in Niger means much more
than the typical seizure of power by the military.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.580
Yes, it is true that Niger is one of the poorest
countries in the world.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.720
But despite this, it did have a recognized
democracy.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.230
It had a government willing to ask for international
help to curb jihadism, which is making the

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.769
Sahel its territory.

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:26.619
In this sense, Niger was the great ally of
the West in the heart of the Sahel.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:31.150
Now, however, all this has been blown to bits
by the coup d'état at the end of July.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.460
Now Niger's military junta is still looking
for foreign help.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.410
But it wants to change allies.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:42.050
(Niger's junta asks for help from Russian
group Wagner as it faces military intervention

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.050
threat – AP NEWS)

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:48.340
But wait a minute, because military intervention
was not offered by any Western power, concerned

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.630
as they are by the Kremlin's growing influence
in Africa.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:57.550
So help was not offered, at least not directly.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:03.059
It was ECOWAS, the Economic Community of West
African States, which is not willing to tolerate

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.940
another military coup and is demanding the
return to power of Mohamed Bazoum, the deposed

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.430
president of Niger.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:15.000
And that is exactly what has set the drums
of war beating in Africa.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:22.150
(10 August 2023: West African Leaders Activate
'Standby Force' to Respond to Niger Coup – NY

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.150
Times)

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.840
Worst of all, this military intervention could
go beyond Niger and trigger a regional conflict

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.079
that could spread to multiple countries.

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:33.500
This is how the spokesman of the military
junta, Colonel Amadou Abdramane, put it;

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:41.570
A pre-deployment of forces to participate
in this war started in two countries of Central

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:42.570
Africa.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:47.790
Faced with the threat of intervention which
is becoming clearer through preparation from

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:50.460
neighboring countries, Niger's airspace is
closed from today)

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.479
Abdramane has not hesitated to accuse a "foreign
power" of instigating and preparing an attack

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:56.500
against Niger.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.400
Of course, he is referring to France, its
former colonial ruler.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.920
In fact, the military junta has broken all
Niger's military agreements with France.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.450
The Macron government merely indicated that
it supports the ECOWAS intervention.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.170
So, you are already seeing how things are
progressing.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:13.750
And you may be wondering: why has this coup
d'état taken place in Niger?

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.870
What role is Russia playing in all this?

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.890
And above all, how many countries might this
conflict end up splattering?

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:24.001
On VisualPolitik today we are going to answer
all these questions, but first, let's take

00:02:24.001 --> 00:02:28.490
a look at a bit of History.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:33.110
(THE LAST DEMOCRACY OF THE SAHEL)

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:40.040
The Sahel is a narrow strip of land south
of the Sahara desert characterized by extreme

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.090
poverty.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:45.420
Four countries are located in the center of
the Sahel, from west to east: Mali, Burkina

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.159
Faso, Niger and Chad.

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:49.170
Well, they all have several things in common.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.870
To begin with, all of these countries are
landlocked; what’s more, French is spoken

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:57.180
in all four, so you can probably guess which
country was the colonial power; they are also

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.170
majority Muslim countries.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.590
And now they also have something else in common:
all of them are currently governed by the

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.670
military after the coup d'état that put an
end to the Seventh Republic of Niger.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:12.640
And yes, more than one of you will be thinking:
but let's see [host], if Niger gained independence

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:18.959
from France in 1960, 63 years with 7 Republics
works out to 9 years per Republic.

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:24.230
Yes, that’s true but stability and Niger
are two words that do not usually go hand

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:28.290
in hand.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.480
Even so, there does appear to have been a
change since 2010.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:36.730
A military coup in favor of democracy ousted
President Mamadou Tandja from power, a man

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.860
who had been elected at the ballot box but
who aspired to keep himself in power and turn

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.040
Niger into an authoritarian regime.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.280
The transition was supported by the international
community and resulted in the Constitution

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.310
of the 7th Republic.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:54.810
A period that in 2021 would see the first
peaceful transfer of power between presidents.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:04:00.129
Nevertheless, in the last decade the Sahel
has seen a serious threat destabilizing the

00:04:00.129 --> 00:04:01.420
entire region.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.420
We are talking about jihadism.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.650
Religious fanaticism finds its soldiers among
the desperate and often starving inhabitants

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:08.840
of these Sahel countries.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:12.670
These are people who were born in one of the
worst places in the world; and the jihadists

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:16.400
promise them a better present and a future
in paradise.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.509
And, of course, the problem is that the alternative
is subsistence agriculture, on which more

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:25.310
than 80% of Niger's population lives in poverty.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:29.630
In fact, extreme poverty reaches almost half
of all the country's inhabitants.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:33.979
These figures have hardly changed in the 13
years of the 7th Republic.

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:37.870
We are talking about data very similar to
those of neighboring countries such as Mali

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.140
and Burkina Faso.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:44.200
Both have had coups d'état in the last three
years that ended democracy: Mali in 2021 and

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.509
Burkina Faso in 2022.

00:04:46.509 --> 00:04:51.060
In both cases, the military seized power under
the pretext of ending jihadism.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.880
However, the results have been quite the opposite.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:58.009
Take a look at this map produced by the US
company StratFor of violent incidents in the

00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:04.970
Sahel between August 2021 and August 2022.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.190
The war against jihadism has triggered violence.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:14.389
In 2022, jihadist deaths in the Sahel increased
by 75%, to more than 10,000.

00:05:14.389 --> 00:05:15.910
Chaos prevails.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.130
And Mali's military junta has turned to the
Wagners.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.889
In Burkina Faso, the government barely controls
40% of the country.

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:26.100
In Niger the situation is not so extreme,
but the same jihadist groups that are ravaging

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.919
Mali and Burkina Faso are also active there.

00:05:28.919 --> 00:05:34.229
We are talking about Al-Qaeda and Daesh affiliates;
it also suffers constant attacks by Boko Haram

00:05:34.229 --> 00:05:37.410
and the Islamic State in its border area with
Nigeria.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:42.300
Yet unlike in Burkina Faso and Mali, the last
year in Niger was proving to be the least

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.789
deadly since 2018.

00:05:43.789 --> 00:05:47.380
So the question is, what is the reason for
this difference?

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:51.930
Well, nothing less than the approach adopted
in Niger by the government of Mohamed Bazoum

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.260
against jihadism.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:55.430
His strategy has several steps:

00:05:55.430 --> 00:06:00.270
First, Western military aid, mainly provided
by France and the United States; second, the

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:05.020
improvement of State services in the most
depressed areas; and third, other initiatives

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:10.729
that are as opposed to the war against jihadism
as they are obviously controversial:

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:15.800
(Niger: Mohamed Bazoum releases "terrorists"
to open the dialogue)

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:20.340
The Bazoum-backed demobilization plan promised
to reintegrate into society jihadists who

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.979
laid down their arms.

00:06:21.979 --> 00:06:27.210
So basically: dialogue in exchange for a truce;
freedom in exchange for peace.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:32.120
From the Western point of view, talking to
terrorists is a bad idea: it implies giving

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:37.550
in to their blackmail and opens the door to
fresh attacks in order to achieve new concessions.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:43.770
However, in a country like Niger, the real
power of the State and the strength of the

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.389
terrorist groups must be weighed against each
other.

00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:50.889
If the fight is balanced, going to war could
be a disaster for the population.

00:06:50.889 --> 00:06:52.730
Other avenues must be explored.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:57.080
And of course, there are those who are not
willing to tolerate the slightest sign of

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.080
weakness.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.650
This is how the new president of Niger, General
Omar Tchiani, justified his coup d'état due

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:08.669
to the alleged deterioration of security caused
by jihadism.

00:07:08.669 --> 00:07:19.650
This is 
the same excuse that the coup plotters gave

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:21.699
in Mali and Burkina Faso.

00:07:21.699 --> 00:07:25.120
But you have already seen that the data from
Niger are quite different.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.590
So there must be something else.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.990
The question is, what?

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:32.479
Well, possibly the pre-coup rumors that General
Tchiani was going to be removed as the head

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:34.500
of the presidential guard are true.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:38.150
Don’t lose sight of the fact that it was
the presidential guard that carried out the

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.699
coup by taking President Bazoum hostage.

00:07:40.699 --> 00:07:43.840
The Army had to declare itself afterwards.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:44.840
Take a look:

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:49.500
(Niger army backs coup against pro-western
leader to prevent 'bloodbath' – FT)

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.169
But well, it is not worth giving much more
thought to all this.

00:07:52.169 --> 00:07:56.180
At the end of the day, they are military men
staging a coup d'état to seize power.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:00.130
Whether out of personal ambition or national
discontent, for one reason or another it is

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:02.440
daily fodder on the African continent.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:05.820
Nevertheless, VisualPolitik community, this
time they have come up against the direct

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.150
rejection of a regional organization such
as ECOWAS.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:13.759
An organization that seems ready to do anything
to restore democracy in Niger.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:18.920
And take note because it would not be the
first time.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:24.349
(ECHOES OF WAR)

00:08:24.349 --> 00:08:31.220
ECOWAS is an organization made up of 15 West
African countries including Niger.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:35.580
Initially it was an organization with an economic
purpose of forming a single trade bloc.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:39.940
But wait a minute, because ECOWAS has also
mobilized peacekeepers in the region and intervened

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.630
in member countries in times of great instability.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:47.160
In the last 30 years they have been active
in Sierra Leone, Guinea Bissau, Ivory Coast,

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:50.920
Liberia, Mali and Gambia.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:56.450
It was in Gambia that the last ECOWAS military
intervention took place, It was in 2017.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:09:01.079
After two decades in power, Yahya Jammeh was
reluctant to relinquish power to Adama Barrow,

00:09:01.079 --> 00:09:02.860
who had won the presidential election.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:07.510
ECOWAS formed a coalition of troops from Senegal,
Ghana and Nigeria and set out to invade The

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:08.510
Gambia.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:14.060
Yahya Jammeh resigned after three days and
democracy was restored).

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:16.210
Even so, Niger is not Gambia.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:20.840
Its territory is 100 times larger and its
armed forces, in addition to being more numerous,

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.150
has years of training by Western forces.

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:27.270
So military intervention is complex and would
involve taking many more risks.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:31.740
The first one, the life of President Bazoum,
who is not in exile but in the hands of the

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:32.900
coup plotters.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:38.800
(Western officials: Niger junta warned they'd
kill deposed president after any military

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.800
intervention – ABC News)

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:43.490
On top of that, I am sure many of you are
wondering why ECOWAS has now been so firm

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:48.019
and assertive towards Niger when similar coups
have also recently taken place in Mali and

00:09:48.019 --> 00:09:50.690
Burkina Faso.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:55.850
Well, the key to everything lies with one
person: Bola Tinubu.

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:59.250
He has been the new president of Nigeria since
last May.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:03.519
Tinubu has had enough time to be appointed
president of ECOWAS at the beginning of July.

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:15.990
A representative position from which he launched
this message at his inauguration:

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:19.740
In his speech he also defended democracy,
freedom and the rule of law.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.240
And all this is much more than Bola Tinubu's
words.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:26.260
They are the new Nigerian president's letter
of introduction to ECOWAS, to the African

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:32.950
continent and even the whole world.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:36.200
After all, we cannot forget the enormous influence
of Nigeria.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.579
We are talking about the great African power
alongside Egypt and South Africa.

00:10:39.579 --> 00:10:42.339
And, naturally, it is the leading voice of
ECOWAS.

00:10:42.339 --> 00:10:46.330
Aside from its concern that Niger will suffer
the same fate as Mali and Burkina Faso and

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:51.149
that violence in the area will escalate, Nigeria
wants to assume its role as a regional leader.

00:10:51.149 --> 00:10:54.860
And the Niger coup took place just three weeks
after Tinubu's speech.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:59.050
So, as long as diplomacy remains unsuccessful,
military preparations will continue.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:02.550
The credibility of Bola Tinubu is at stake.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:07.519
(ECOWAS contingent for invasion of Niger may
amount up to 25,000 – RFI)

00:11:07.519 --> 00:11:10.380
More than half of the contingent would be
contributed by Nigeria.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:13.990
Senegal, Ivory Coast and Benin have also confirmed
that they will send troops.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:18.040
And then there are two other countries with
troops on the ground: one is France.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:22.050
The former colonial ruler is being used by
the coup plotters as a scapegoat.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:24.420
Everything that is wrong in Niger is France's
fault.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:27.880
Indeed, the coup plotters have attacked the
French embassy and even accused the Macron

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.950
government of releasing terrorists.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:33.210
On top of that, we don’t want to show unpleasant
images, but just to let you know that the

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:37.430
coup plotters filled a soccer stadium and
people cheered along as they decapitated a

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.730
rooster painted with the French flag.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:46.970
Surely with all this you already have an idea
of the animosity they have towards France.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:52.560
Well, the Gauls maintain a permanent base
there, equipped with fighter jets, Reaper

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.110
drones and 1,500 troops.

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:58.709
The Macron government has said it supports
ECOWAS efforts to return Bazoum to power.

00:11:58.709 --> 00:12:02.970
However, chances are that not a single French
soldier will move, lest the military junta

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:07.600
is here to stay and agreements such as the
one of last May will need to be revised.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:13.269
(Niger: agreement signed with the French Orano
for the exploitation of uranium deposits until

00:12:13.269 --> 00:12:14.510
2040)

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:19.209
It is clear that France's interest is to continue
exploiting uranium from Niger, which has been

00:12:19.209 --> 00:12:21.820
its third largest supplier in recent decades.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:25.170
Then, the other country that has troops in
Niger is the United States.

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:29.000
In total there are more than a thousand troops,
deployed in several drone bases.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:32.250
For the moment, the White House is betting
on the diplomatic route.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.930
But it is being asked to take action.

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:40.360
(Niger's ousted leader says he's a hostage
and urges U.S. to halt coup – NBC News)

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:44.610
The former president asked for it in a letter
to the Washington Post, no less.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:49.130
Yes, it seems difficult to understand, what
kind of coup perpetrators allow their prisoner

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.519
to communicate freely with the outside world?

00:12:51.519 --> 00:12:55.329
Because following the coup, Bazoum posted
a tweet and has even spoken on the phone with

00:12:55.329 --> 00:13:00.610
Blinken, with Charles Michel, with Borrell...
come on, he was almost a YouTuber.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:04.060
Nevertheless, neither the White House nor
the European Union are making progress in

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.440
negotiations with Niger's military junta.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:10.790
The coup leaders have even refused to receive
a tripartite delegation composed of representatives

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.751
of ECOWAS, the African Union and the UN.

00:13:12.751 --> 00:13:14.050
And do you know what?

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:18.000
The military is very clear about what they
want Niger's place in the world to be and

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.170
who will be its allies.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:27.580
Listen up.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:32.829
(BEYOND THE WALL)

00:13:32.829 --> 00:13:39.160
The military juntas of Mali and Burkina Faso
offer us the playbook to be followed by the

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:40.899
modern African coup plotter:

00:13:40.899 --> 00:13:45.310
The first thing is to attack the former colonial
power in every possible way.

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:47.100
They have to be blamed for everything.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:50.690
In the case of Niger, for example, we have
already shown you some examples.

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:54.190
But wait a moment, because they can still
do more against France.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:58.190
In Mali, for example, they eliminated French
as an official language and both here and

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:01.839
in Burkina Faso they expelled all the French
troops that were there fighting jihadism.

00:14:01.839 --> 00:14:04.899
[sarcastic tone] So just a couple of tweaks.

00:14:04.899 --> 00:14:09.070
Be that as it may, the next step would be
to take positions within this multipolar world.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.990
And in Niger, they have already made their
choice.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:15.529
(Niger's tailors rush to make Russian flags
after coup – Reuters)

00:14:15.529 --> 00:14:19.310
The coup plotters have created a swathe of
military-led countries in Africa stretching

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.350
from the Atlantic Ocean to the Red Sea.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:24.750
Most of these countries are now more aligned
with Russia than with the West.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:29.620
Not only that, but they intend to build a
wall against the once undisputed Western influence.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:33.329
VisualPolitik community, neither Russia nor
Wagner are involved in the preparations for

00:14:33.329 --> 00:14:34.570
the coup d'état in Niger.

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:37.839
But once it has taken place, both are ready
to profit from it.

00:14:37.839 --> 00:14:45.070
Wagner is spreading throughout Africa like
a virus.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:48.450
In fact, before the Prigozhin mutiny, the
mercenaries of the Wagner group were part

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:52.460
of the catalog of services offered by Russia
in its diplomatic negotiations.

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:55.790
This is how Wagner is creating a presence
in countries such as the Republic of Mali,

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:59.800
where authoritarian regimes hire Prigozhin's
men to do their dirty work.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:05.180
Meanwhile, the Kremlin displaces the West
as the influential power in the area.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:11.889
Putin is very interested in Africa, as demonstrated
at the summit just held in St. Petersburg.

00:15:11.889 --> 00:15:16.230
So all indications are that Prigozhin will
continue his operations on the African continent

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:19.240
as long as he remains useful for Putin's purposes.

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:22.759
And you saw at the beginning of the video
that Niger's military junta has asked the

00:15:22.759 --> 00:15:24.070
Wagner Group for help.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:28.490
A group that has taken control of the gold
and diamond mines in the Central African Republic,

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:30.010
in Mali, in Sudan.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.680
And what does Niger have for Wagner?

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.870
Well, mainly uranium.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:38.139
Depriving Europe of uranium from Niger would
bring a smile to the faces of Putin and Prigozhin,

00:15:38.139 --> 00:15:41.100
but it does not seem so attractive to Russian
mercenaries.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.320
Something else is needed.

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:45.020
And well, Niger does have the occasional gold
mine.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.260
And it also has oil.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:51.699
In fact, Niger was aiming for a 5-fold increase
in its modest crude oil production this year.

00:15:51.699 --> 00:15:55.690
The thing is, as those of you who are regulars
on VisualPolitik know, Wagner is always out

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:56.709
to make a profit.

00:15:56.709 --> 00:15:59.319
Still, this is the least of the military junta's
concerns.

00:15:59.319 --> 00:16:02.490
The ECOWAS intervention is their number one
priority now.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:06.430
And everything indicates that in the case
that the intervention finally does take place,

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:09.980
the coup plotters in Niger would not be on
their own.

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:15.769
(Burkina Faso, Mali say military intervention
in Niger would be 'declaration of war' – France24)

00:16:15.769 --> 00:16:18.550
The walls of the coup plotters are being fortified.

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:23.630
And take note because Algeria and Guinea have
also shown their rejection of military intervention.

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:27.060
Meanwhile ECOWAS continues to put pressure
on Tchiani's military junta by ordering the

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:31.450
mobilization of its reserve force to restore
constitutional order in Niger.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:35.360
This conflict threatens to directly involve
a lot of African countries that have already

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:38.620
stated they will take up arms to defend their
positions.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:41.709
On VisualPolitik we will continue to follow
this budding conflict.

00:16:41.709 --> 00:16:46.120
But now the questions are for you: Do you
think ECOWAS will succeed in restoring democracy

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.120
in Niger?

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:50.009
Will any power outside the African continent
get directly involved?

00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:51.820
Leave us your answer in the comments.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:56.080
If you found this video interesting, please
like and share it with your friends.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.860
All the best and see you next time.

